// aephysics.dynamics -- the world's state and its bookkeeping: the
// world with its sparse arrays of bodies, shapes, contacts, joints and
// islands (each keyed by a recycled id with a generation, so a stale id
// is caught), the solver sets that keep the simulation data of static,
// disabled, awake and sleeping bodies in contiguous arrays, the islands
// that group bodies by their constraints, the shapes' place in the
// broad phase, and the mass properties of a body from its shapes.
// Nothing here steps time: the solver and the world's step are the
// layers above.
//
// This is the organisational half of Box3D's body.c, shape.c,
// solver_set.c, island.c and physics_world.c (Erin Catto, MIT), the
// reference this engine is measured against: a body is an entry in a
// sparse array pointing at its sim (and, when awake, its state) inside
// a solver set; the static set holds static bodies, the disabled set
// disabled ones, the awake set everything simulated, and each sleeping
// island is a set of its own; a shape lives in a doubly linked list on
// its body and in the broad phase's tree of its body's type. Names are
// the reference's without its prefix, in snake case: b3CreateBody is
// create_body, b3Body_SetMassData is body_set_mass_data.
//
// This layer: worlds, bodies (creation, destruction, transforms,
// velocities, mass data, extents, damping, sleep and enable flags, the
// type changed, disabled and enabled), shapes (creation of every kind,
// destruction, proxies), contacts (the pair filter, the narrow phase,
// the touching state, the events), the constraint graph, islands, solver
// sets (sleep, wake, merge), joints (the base of every kind, their
// creation on two bodies with the edges, sets and islands, destruction,
// the accessors, separations and reactions; the solving of the kinds
// comes with joint_solver), sensors (their overlaps begin and end), and
// the validation. Nothing here steps time.
//
// The hull database is the reference's: a hull shape holds the world's
// copy of its hull, shared by every shape of an equal hull and freed with
// its last, so a caller may free its hull once the shape is made.
// Differences: no name cache, no recording hooks; a world's callbacks are
// plain function values.
